<title>USA: Florida puts $300 million deal on 20-hour notice.</title>
<headline>Florida puts $300 million deal on 20-hour notice.</headline>
<dateline>TALLAHASSEE, Fla. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida will sell $300 million of Preservation 2000 revenue bonds by competitive bid with 20-hours notice, the state Division of Bond Finance said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bonds are designated Florida Department of Environmental Protection Preservation 2000 revenue bonds, series 1997A. The bonds finance the purchase of environmentally sensitive land are repaid with documentary stamp tax receipts.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
